  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int \\frac{d x}{\\cos x+\\sqrt{3} \\sin x}$\n$=\\frac{1}{2} \\int \\sec \\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) d x$\n$=\\frac{1}{2} \\log \\tan \\left(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+c$\n$=\\frac{1}{2} \\log \\tan \\left(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)+c$."
  }
